================================================================================
SCOPE — WHAT THIS LICENCE DOES AND DOES NOT COVER
================================================================================

The MIT grant above covers the code and configuration in this repository: the
Python pipeline in `src/`, `scripts/` and `tools/`, the site's HTML, CSS and
JavaScript in `site/` (outside the carve-outs below), the tests and smoke
checks, the prototypes' code, and the CI workflows.

It does NOT cover the three carve-outs below. Two of them are not mine to
license, and the third is licensed separately on purpose.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CARVE-OUT 1 — PROSE: CC BY 4.0
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    docs/
    README.md
    CONTRIBUTING.md
    TODO.md
    data/DATA.md
    session-summary/
    prototype/README.md

The written material (specs, decision records, source notes, methodology) is
licensed Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International, not MIT. See
`LICENSE-docs`.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CARVE-OUT 2 — OPEN GOVERNMENT DATA: NOT MINE TO LICENSE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    site/public/data/
    data/name_variants.csv

Every data file here is derived from public releases and remains subject to
its upstream terms. I hold no copyright in them and grant none.

  - City of Edmonton sources (wards, school wards, addresses, building
    rooflines, council contacts, election results)
    Open Government Licence – City of Edmonton
    https://data.edmonton.ca/stories/s/City-of-Edmonton-Open-Data-Terms-of-Use/msh8-if28/

  - Government of Alberta provincial electoral divisions
    Open Government Licence – Alberta
    https://open.alberta.ca/licence

  - Elections Canada federal electoral districts; NRCan MRDEM-30 elevation
    Open Government Licence – Canada
    https://open.canada.ca/en/open-government-licence-canada

  - Names of office holders and links to their official pages, from the
    Legislative Assembly of Alberta, the House of Commons and the two school
    boards. These publishers state no licence on the pages used; the records
    are public facts about who holds an office, and each links back to its
    source of record.

Per-source provenance is in `data/DATA.md`. If you reuse this data, the
attribution obligation runs to those publishers directly, not through me. The
prescribed attribution statements, which are verbatim compliance text and must
not be reworded, are on the site's About page and pinned by
`tests/test_site_build.py`.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CARVE-OUT 3 — THIRD-PARTY LIBRARIES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    site/public/licenses/

The built site bundles maplibre-gl and pmtiles (both BSD-3-Clause) from npm,
at the exact versions in `package-lock.json`. Their licence texts ship in
`site/public/licenses/`, because the minifier strips the notices from the
bundle.

================================================================================

The carve-out paths above are the authoritative list. `tests/test_license.py`
reads them out of this file and fails if a data-shaped file is committed
outside them.
